@startuml
' Figure 39.5  Rollback with runs in flight
' Reading order: top to bottom, Thursday, July 30, 2026, 8:40 a.m.
' CDT. The release owner rolls R-0723 back; the router sends queued
' refunds to the parent bundle; started runs restart there; approval
' cards bound to the old proposal are cancelled and re-proposed; runs
' awaiting a verdict go to the reconciler; done runs are audited by
' bundle hash. From release.rollback.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Owner" as O <<org>>
participant "Router" as R <<ops>>
participant "R-0723 runs" as A <<fail>>
participant "Reconciler" as V <<evidence>>
O -[$FAIL]> R : Roll back
R -> R : 4 queued
R -> A : 7 restart
A -> R : 6 re-propose
A -> V : 23 verdicts
V -> O : 59 audited
note over R, A $F_OPS : 17 trail lines
@enduml
